The problem with this technique is that putting stuff in a sack while 
in a store
counts the same as carrying it *even* if you then drop the sack. That's
why the shopkeeper called the guards after you left the store -- as far as
he knew, you were carrying unpaid potions.
If you really want to rob shops with this kind of (possible) abuse, just
acquire a valuable gem, and sell it to the shopkeeper repeatedly, kicking it
out after each sale, until you have enough cash simply to *buy* all the
potions. For that matter, you could use the much-discussed infinite-gold
bug. All of these techniques are abusive to varying degrees.
(Please route all discussion of what is an abuse and what is within the
scope of the game to talk.useless.annoying.)

> 6. To battle a leprechaun just drop your gold and have at em.

You have to drop the gold *outside* the room the leprechaun is in, or he will
try to run over and pick it up. If you stand on the spot with the gold,
he grabs it from between your legs. In a bind, it is helpful to throw your
gold out the door.

